## Optional and host services (not bundled)

These services are separate processes (or, for Qt, dynamically linked) and are
never copied into the MIT codebase. None is a hard dependency: the core desktop
installs, starts, and works without them, and every feature has an absence
path. Packaging marks them `Recommends` or `Suggests`, never `Requires`; the
marker table is [packaging/optional-services.json](packaging/optional-services.json)
(ADR [0229](docs/design/adr/0229-naming-and-optional-service-decisions.md)).

| Capability | Component | License | Integration |
|---|---|---|---|
| Search (optional backend) | Tracker | GPL-2.0-or-later | separate process (D-Bus) |
| Search (optional backend) | Baloo | LGPL-2.1-or-later | separate process (D-Bus) |
| Search (optional backend) | Recoll | GPL-2.0-or-later | separate process (CLI/D-Bus) |
| Backup (preferred backend) | restic | BSD-2-Clause | CLI/JSON |
| Backup (optional delegate) | Pika Backup | GPL-3.0-or-later | separate app |
| Backup (optional delegate) | Timeshift | GPL-3.0-or-later | separate app |
| Online accounts | GNOME Online Accounts | LGPL-2.1-or-later | separate process (D-Bus) |
| Accessibility | Orca | LGPL-2.1-or-later | separate process (AT-SPI) |
| Accessibility | speech-dispatcher | GPL-2.0-or-later | separate process (API) |
| Accessibility (optional synthesizer) | espeak-ng | GPL-3.0-or-later | separate process (CLI/API) |
| Input methods | ibus | LGPL-2.1-or-later | separate process (D-Bus/API) |
| Input methods | fcitx5 | LGPL-2.1-or-later | separate process (D-Bus/API) |
| Firewall (Fedora family) | firewalld | GPL-2.0-or-later | separate process (D-Bus) |
